01:16:11.484 --> 01:16:13.020
- Did you find him?
- Yeah.


01:16:13.569 --> 01:16:15.105
How'd it go?


01:16:15.321 --> 01:16:18.280
- I did most of the talking.
- Well, good.


01:16:18.491 --> 01:16:20.357
At least you got it
all out there.


01:16:22.286 --> 01:16:23.242
Almost.


01:16:27.583 --> 01:16:30.451
I don't think we can live
together anymore.


01:16:31.420 --> 01:16:34.003
It's me. I'm a mess.


01:16:34.215 --> 01:16:36.502
I need to get my shit together.


01:16:37.593 --> 01:16:41.382
And I can't, if I keep letting
you bail me out of everything.


01:16:42.431 --> 01:16:45.799
You're too good to me.
I don't know why...


01:16:46.018 --> 01:16:49.477
'cause I can be a real asshole
to you sometimes.


01:16:49.688 --> 01:16:54.023
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, we are now
boarding flight</i> 770 <i>to Seattle.</i>


01:16:54.193 --> 01:16:56.480
<i>Please have your
boarding passes ready.</i>


01:17:03.702 --> 01:17:04.738
This doesn't mean...


01:17:04.954 --> 01:17:06.411
- that we won't see each other.
- No, of course not.


01:17:06.622 --> 01:17:08.113
You're the most important
person in my life.


01:17:08.332 --> 01:17:09.573
You are, too,
ever since fifth grade.


01:17:09.792 --> 01:17:12.375
- We'll see each other as much as ever.
- Probably more. Yeah.


01:17:13.420 --> 01:17:16.163
Okay. Yeah.


01:17:26.392 --> 01:17:30.181
Wait. You're an amazing person,
and you always have been.


01:17:30.855 --> 01:17:33.017
I've always wanted
to be more like you.


01:17:34.233 --> 01:17:36.646
If anything,
I rely on you too much.


01:17:47.746 --> 01:17:49.738
I always cry at transitions.


01:18:07.975 --> 01:18:09.432
Miss Jeffries!


01:18:09.643 --> 01:18:12.807
Oh, hi, Demerius.
You're here early.


01:18:12.980 --> 01:18:15.723
Computer club.
I, um, did the report.


01:18:15.941 --> 01:18:17.933
You said two pages?


01:18:18.152 --> 01:18:20.610
So, is it okay that
I did it like that?


01:18:20.779 --> 01:18:23.522
- You drew this?
- Yeah, I finished the book.


01:18:24.325 --> 01:18:27.033
What they did to Piggy?
That was whack.


01:18:27.244 --> 01:18:29.361
Yeah, that was absolutely whack.


01:18:29.580 --> 01:18:31.492
So, is it okay?


01:18:31.707 --> 01:18:34.324
Yeah, it's okay.


01:18:34.543 --> 01:18:36.500
Miss Jeffries, hold up a second!


01:18:37.546 --> 01:18:39.879
- All right, I'll see you in class.
- See you in class.


01:18:40.090 --> 01:18:41.547
Gosh, you look great.


01:18:41.759 --> 01:18:44.092
Will you stop it?
I'm not gonna quit my job.


01:18:44.303 --> 01:18:45.714
Who asked you to quit your job?


01:18:45.930 --> 01:18:47.091
- You did.
- No, I didn't.


01:18:47.306 --> 01:18:48.513
- Yes, you did.
- No.


01:18:48.724 --> 01:18:50.090
I'll check my notes, but I'm...


01:18:50.309 --> 01:18:52.016
I'm pretty sure you
misunderstood me.


01:18:52.228 --> 01:18:55.596
No, on the contrary,
I'm here to offer you...


01:18:55.814 --> 01:18:58.227
the assistant volleyball
coach position.


01:18:58.943 --> 01:19:01.560
Mrs. Garcia's out
on maternity leave.


01:19:01.737 --> 01:19:03.069
Did you know she was pregnant?


01:19:03.280 --> 01:19:05.397
- No.
- Neither did I.


01:19:06.492 --> 01:19:09.405
Uh, well, just think about it.
Get back to me, okay?


01:19:13.374 --> 01:19:15.787
- Principle Moss!
- I can't, I got a board...


01:19:16.001 --> 01:19:18.163
No, no, come here,
I want you to see this.


01:19:18.379 --> 01:19:20.587
Demerius, that kid with
the comic, he did this.


01:19:20.798 --> 01:19:22.915
This is amazing. Look at that.


01:19:24.510 --> 01:19:26.752
You know what?
I was thinking about it over break...


01:19:26.971 --> 01:19:28.382
and I wanna shift the paradigm...


01:19:28.597 --> 01:19:30.634
of the left-brained
didactic teaching structure...


01:19:30.849 --> 01:19:34.183
to a more right-brained,
outside-the-box learning style.


01:19:34.395 --> 01:19:35.636
Do you follow?


01:19:35.854 --> 01:19:36.970
- I...
- I'm so sorry.


01:19:37.189 --> 01:19:39.681
It's such a bore when people
talk like assholes, isn't it?


01:19:40.234 --> 01:19:42.567
What I'm trying to say
is I want your support...


01:19:42.736 --> 01:19:45.194
to do more stuff like this.
Oh, and you know what?


01:19:45.406 --> 01:19:47.898
I looked into cutting hair
and you are absolutely right.


01:19:48.784 --> 01:19:50.776
Hairdressers make
a goddamn fortune.


01:19:50.995 --> 01:19:53.203
It almost sounds like
you're threatening me.


01:19:53.414 --> 01:19:57.875
Stanley... Stan... relax.
We are on the same team, here.


01:19:58.085 --> 01:20:01.999
I am just trying to keep
your instructional scaffolding in place.


01:20:02.214 --> 01:20:04.501
Especially right before testing.


01:20:05.509 --> 01:20:07.796
Oh, and you know what?


01:20:08.012 --> 01:20:11.221
Yes to volleyball.
Sounds like an adventure.


01:20:11.890 --> 01:20:13.426
Go Falcons!


01:20:16.562 --> 01:20:18.679
Edgeworth, he brought math
to economics.


01:20:18.897 --> 01:20:21.230
He wrote the essay on
application of math...


01:20:21.442 --> 01:20:23.650
to moral science, 1881.


01:20:23.861 --> 01:20:27.730
Leon Morris...
Theory of General Competitive-


01:20:27.948 --> 01:20:29.109
Hold on.


01:20:30.784 --> 01:20:35.028
Hello? Yes. I know, I know.
I'll be there.


01:20:35.247 --> 01:20:37.239
<i>- Who is it?</i>
- Sorry, it was Kate.


01:20:37.458 --> 01:20:40.371
<i>Well, you know, I gotta get to
bed anyway. I'll see you later?</i>


01:20:40.586 --> 01:20:41.667
Sixteen days.


01:20:41.837 --> 01:20:43.703
<i>Sixteen days.</i>


01:20:45.257 --> 01:20:46.873
<i>Give me something
to dream about.</i>


01:20:47.509 --> 01:20:49.250
Oh, you scamp.


01:20:49.470 --> 01:20:50.551
<i>Come on.</i>


01:20:51.347 --> 01:20:52.929
<i>Oh my goodness!</i>


01:20:53.557 --> 01:20:55.970
<i>Oh boy. You are the mo...</i>


01:21:17.456 --> 01:21:18.492
Hey.


01:21:23.796 --> 01:21:25.753
I'm here. Has it started?


01:21:26.673 --> 01:21:28.835
<i>I don't think that Kalynn's
going any farther.</i>


01:21:30.552 --> 01:21:31.542
<i>She's cracking.</i>


01:21:33.555 --> 01:21:36.423
<i>This is too hard.
I don't know if I can...</i>


01:21:36.642 --> 01:21:38.304
Who acts like that?

